When I first started building, I skipped writing technical docs because it felt like wasted time. I thought I would remember how the authentication logic worked three months later.

I was wrong. When I had to update our shipping integration recently, I spent an hour trying to decipher my own messy code. I ended up creating an internal notes doc for our architecture to stop the cycle of constant confusion.

What is your go-to strategy for maintaining technical documentation while building fast?

